# Built C test binaries and helpers (tests/Makefile $(TESTS) + its object
# targets). Listed as a CLASS, not one line per test: the per-file list had
# drifted by 33 of the 64 products tests/Makefile builds, and because
# scripts/tree-hash.sh hashes tracked PLUS untracked-but-unignored files, each
# missing name silently changed the tree hash as soon as anyone ran
# `make -C tests`. That is what broke the pairing of demo-rehearsal counted
# attempt 2 (hash c47f9d0f vs attempt 1's d645b0ee).
#
# The rule is the FILENAME SUFFIX, so state it as one instead of guessing
# prefixes. `tests/*` catches every direct child; the negations give back
# the two kinds that are real content -- anything with a suffix
# (tests/foo.c, .py, .sh, .mjs, .list) and every subdirectory
# (tests/fixtures/, tests/web_unit/, ...). What stays ignored is exactly
# "a direct child of tests/ with no suffix", which is what a linker emits.
#
# Prefix classes were the first attempt and they drifted within one merge:
# tests/open_ckpt_stub and tests/trace_closure_probe arrived from
# agent/424-durability matching none of test_*, wait_cpu_*, gen_*, bench_*.
# tests/test_gitignore_build_products.sh caught it, which is the whole
# reason that test exists.
#
# tests/Makefile is the only suffix-less file in tests/ that is TRACKED, so
# it is the only negation that has to name something. Add a `!` line for any
# future one; the guard above will tell you, by name, the moment there is.
tests/*
!tests/*.*
!tests/*/
!tests/Makefile
# ...and back on the ignore side, the two shapes the negations overreach to:
# object files and the macOS debug bundle a test binary is built with both
# carry a suffix.
tests/*.o
tests/*.dSYM/
# Python bytecode, at ANY depth. It used to be anchored to tests/, which left
# tests/results/**/__pycache__/*.pyc untracked-but-not-ignored and therefore
# INSIDE scripts/tree-hash.sh's scope: check.sh's py_compile step generated it,
# so a passing `make check` stamp silently depended on bytecode and deleting a
# .pyc invalidated the stamp. Bytecode is never content.
__pycache__/

# Visual-snapshot diff/actual artifacts (transient — only baselines are tracked)
tests/web_snapshots/*-actual.png
tests/web_snapshots/*-diff.png
tests/web_snapshots/gallery/*-actual.png
tests/web_snapshots/gallery/*-diff.png

