# Demo-rehearsal run artifacts, as a CLASS in all four spellings the scripts
# actually use (hyphen/underscore x hidden/visible). Per-file entries here
# are what disqualified counted attempt 2: the per-run provenance file
# tests/results/.demo-rehearsal-provenance-<run_id>.json was never listed,
# so it sat untracked-but-unignored, scripts/tree-hash.sh counted it, the
# provenance hash stopped matching and the attempt was lost -- while its
# sibling .demo-rehearsal-state.sh WAS listed and caused no trouble. Naming
# one more file would leave the next sibling to do it again, and only two
# counted attempts remain.
#
# These are anchored patterns, so `*` does not cross a `/`: they match direct
# children of tests/results/ only. tests/results/probe-bounds/*rehearsal*.txt
# is TRACKED and unaffected -- verified with `git ls-files`, not assumed.
tests/results/demo-rehearsal*
tests/results/demo_rehearsal*
tests/results/.demo-rehearsal*
tests/results/.demo_rehearsal*

# Agent-written evidence directories under tests/results/, ignored AS A
# CLASS instead of one line per directory name (issue: the demo-rehearsal
# patterns above already show the per-name approach falling behind -- an
# agent invents a new directory name, it sits untracked-but-unignored, and
# scripts/tree-hash.sh (tracked + untracked-UNIGNORED) counts it, moving the
# tree hash out from under a counted rehearsal attempt exactly like the
# per-file provenance miss above did). This ignores every directory
# directly under tests/results/ -- `*` does not cross `/`, so this does NOT
# touch tests/results/<file> (tracked top-level files like
# tests/results/gesture_gate.json, tests/results/overhead_trend.csv,
# tests/results/HANDOVER-424.md and tests/results/RELEASE-PLAN.md are
# untouched) and does NOT touch nested files inside a directory this file
# re-tracks below.
#
# A real, intentionally-committed evidence directory is excluded from this
# ignore (re-tracked) by name, below. Verify any change here with
# `git ls-files -i -c --exclude-standard` (must print NOTHING -- a tracked
# file that is also ignored is invisible to `git status` while git still
# tracks it, which is worse than the drift this fixes) BEFORE committing;
# add the new `!tests/results/<dir>/` line in the SAME commit that commits
# real content into a brand new directory, never pre-emptively, and never
# for a directory an agent run merely produced.
tests/results/*/
!tests/results/block-agg/
!tests/results/cpufilter/
!tests/results/cx340-safety/
!tests/results/demo_walk/
!tests/results/gate-integrity/
!tests/results/interference-bounds/
